    + "// reaches.** It sees the whole prelude, and a vector literal, bracket, pattern,\n"
    + "// or `Vector.` call written here would make the emitted `VectorTrie.js` import\n"
    + "// `Vector.js`, which already imports this one — a module cycle nothing in the\n"
    + "// compiler would report, because it is created at emission and not by any\n"
    + "// `import` item. `vector-trie-wiring.test.ts` pins the emitted module's import\n"
    + "// list empty, which is that rule made checkable.\n"
    + "\n"
    + "// A trie node is either a leaf holding up to 32 values, or a branch holding up\n"
    + "// to 32 child subtrees. Both are 32-slot `Node`s; which slots are populated is\n"
    + "// tracked by the enclosing `TrieVector`'s count, never by reading empty slots.\n"
    + "union Tree(a) =\n"
    + "    | Leaf(values: Node(a))\n"
    + "    | Branch(children: Node(Tree(a)))\n"
    + "\n"
    + "// The Vector representation, following Immutable.js's List. Elements live in a\n"
    + "// virtual internal index space; `origin` is the internal index of logical\n"
    + "// element 0 and `capacity` the internal index just past the last, so the logical\n"
    + "// size is `capacity - origin`. `root` addresses the internal range `[0, radix^height)`;\n"
    + "// the `tail` buffer holds the internal range `[tailOffset(capacity), capacity)`\n"
    + "// (its final up-to-32 elements), and the tree holds `[0, tailOffset(capacity))`.\n"
    + "// `height` counts `root`'s levels: 1 => a `Leaf`, 2 => a `Branch` of leaves.\n"
    + "//\n"
